  {
    "episode_id": 96836,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/6/96836.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 9,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, so we're lucky. We have We have a couple farms within a few miles apart. And it's amazing when you're a farmer how you pay attention to the weather in a way that really no one else does. And so we had a couple of thunderstorms brew up over the last couple of days that touched one of our farms and not another. So we've had to make a few different little planting decisions based on where the rain was. But overall, soil conditions are great. Planting has been working out great. Really just Awesome opportunities for us to watch that fifth generation hop in the tractors over the weekend and work some land and get the bug for farming at a young age. So it's been great. We're very blessed.",
